Item 3: kept backing not freed after a client-boundary re-init with no later render
(Greptile P1, Marcelo)

Uncommitted in .claude/worktrees/stack177-review on top of a2e8b5d193b6; item3.diff = `git diff`.

FINDING
With more than half the maximum posted, the 50 ms path of reclaim_check() sets recovery.reinit
and keeps the backing. From then on reclaim_check() and reclaim_delay_ns() both return early on
recovery.reinit, so the 1 s free never runs (and no poll is armed for it) until the next render.
An idle machine after a heavy client keeps up to the whole 512 MiB.

VALIDATION OF THE FINDING: real.
The growth harness now runs the actual reclaim_check(), free_backing(), reclaim_delay_ns(),
note_idle() and Pools::free_chunks(), plus params pb_reclaim()/pb_idle_ns()/pb_reclaim_blocks()
with their asahi_core.rs defaults, and a model of the idle poll work exactly as poll.rs arms it
(each idle pass: note_idle(), reclaim_check(); re-arm for reclaim_delay_ns() rounded up to ms
plus one 4 ms jiffy; stop when None; panic "poll woke in a loop" after 8 wakes).
New case client_boundary_reinit_frees_without_a_render: one VM grows to 2100 posted (18
chunks), its last flight retires, nothing renders after.
Against the pre-fix code (mutation old-reinit-guards: both guards back to `|| self.recovery.reinit`,
which is the old behaviour; the free_backing() refactor is behaviour-neutral):
  FAILED client_boundary_reinit_frees_without_a_render:
  "kept backing not freed: 18 chunks, wakes [54] ms"
i.e. one wake at 54 ms (the re-init), then nothing armed, 18 chunks (288 MiB) held for good.

FIX
pools.rs:
- Pools gains `reclaim_pending: bool` ("the pending re-initialization was set by a reclaim, not a
  recovery"), set where reclaim_check() sets recovery.reinit, cleared in Pools::init() next to
  the ledger reset (the InitBM path, also recovery's).
- reclaim_check(): the early return is `recovery.reinit && !reclaim_pending` (a recovery's
  pending re-init still stops it). With a reclaim's re-init pending, it only does the free:
  at level 2, when Ledger::pending_free_due(idle, g15_pb_idle_ms) holds, it frees the chunks
  above keep_chunks() and logs "PB heap: idle N ms with P blocks posted and the
  re-initialization pending: F chunks freed, B backed"; it does not count another reclaim or
  set anything. The free + VM unmap moved into a helper free_backing(), used by both paths
  (same statements as before).
- reclaim_delay_ns(): same guard; with a reclaim's re-init pending it returns
  Ledger::pending_free_delay(level, idle, g15_pb_idle_ms) = the REMAINING long-idle time
  (not the expired 50 ms), or None at level < 2 or when nothing is above the kept chunks.
- module doc: one clause.
growth.rs:
- pending_free_due(idle, min_idle) = idle >= min_idle && backed > keep_chunks() * CHUNK_BLOCKS
  (keep_chunks, not chunks_for(posted): the posted count drops to the initial size at the
  InitBM, so the posted count must not hold the backing).
- pending_free_delay(level, idle, min_idle).
- unit test pending_reinit_frees_kept_backing.
Harness (tools/asahi/g15-pb-growth-tests.py): the extraction above; model gains Engine.pending
/frozen, Recovery.armed/failed(), a VM Registry with open() (failure injectable, FAIL_OPEN, for
item 7), Pools.idle/reclaim_pending, stats.reclaims/freed, a monotonic clock NOW; LEDGER_RESET
also checks `self.reclaim_pending = false;` in Pools::init(). New cases:
- client_boundary_reinit_frees_without_a_render: wakes exactly [54, 1004] ms after the idle
  began, 2 chunks left (backed 256), freed = chunks - 2, every freed chunk unmapped from the VM
  and its object freed, posted count unchanged (reset waits for the InitBM), recovery.reinit
  and reclaim_pending still set, then at +100 s reclaim_check() does nothing and
  reclaim_delay_ns() is None (no loop);
- client_boundary_reinit_at_level_1_keeps_the_backing: one wake, nothing armed after, a job
  arriving 5 s later (reclaim_check) frees nothing;
- idle_reclaim_arms_nothing_after: the ordinary 1 s reclaim below half the maximum: wakes
  [1004], frees to 2 chunks, nothing armed after;
- recovery_reinit_frees_nothing: reinit set without a reclaim: no wake, nothing freed even
  after 5 s.
New mutations (intended test, message): old-reinit-guards (client_boundary..., "kept backing
not freed"); pending-reinit-stops-free (only the check's guard reverted -> "poll woke in a
loop": the delay is armed but the check never acts, a real wake loop); pending-reinit-arms-
nothing (only the delay's guard -> "kept backing not freed"); pending-delay-from-drain (arm for
the 50 ms -> "poll woke in a loop"); pending-free-at-level-1 (level_1 case, "freed at level 1");
reclaim-pending-not-set ("kept backing not freed"); free-on-recovery-reinit
(recovery_reinit_frees_nothing, "freed for a recovery").

Item boundary: the harness extraction of reclaim_check()/reclaim_delay_ns() is part of item 5
(Chris) as well; it is done here because item 3's test needs it. Item 5 will still replace the
old `Pools::drop_chunks()` model (immediate ledger reset) used by freed_chunks_are_mapped_again
and add its 60 ms / 1.1 s / compute-only cases.

