PLANNED COMMIT: fixup into 29eba03c0d75 "drm/asahi: g15: m3: run the PB reclaim check after the
idle time without new work" (the commit that claims the reclaim runs after idle time without new
work; reclaim_delay_ns() is introduced there, and every piece used exists by then). Per-commit
build and host tests over the rewritten range after the squash. Message changes:
- replace "Nothing is armed while busy, while a re-initialization or a recovery is pending, or
  when nothing can become due." with:
  "Nothing is armed while busy, while a recovery or its re-initialization is pending, or when
  nothing can become due. While a reclaim's re-initialization is pending (a client-boundary
  one keeps the backing), the check still frees the backing above the kept chunks once the
  engine has been idle for g15_pb_idle_ms, and the poll is armed for the rest of that idle,
  not for the expired 50 ms: a heavy client that exits with no render after it otherwise kept
  its backing until the next render."
- add a paragraph after the growth.rs host-test paragraph:
  "The growth harness also runs reclaim_check(), free_backing(), reclaim_delay_ns() and
  note_idle(), driven as the idle poll work arms them: a heavy client that exits with nothing
  rendered after it is re-initialized after 50 ms and its kept backing freed after the long
  idle, with two wakes and nothing armed after; at level 1 the backing stays; a recovery's
  pending re-initialization frees nothing."

